.TH EUCLID-CLI-ENS-STOP-TOPIC 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.73" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ens-stop-topic \- stop delivering a topic's messages to its subscribers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ens stop-topic
.BR \-\-topic | \-t
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stops handing a topic's messages to its subscribers.
.PP
Publishing carries on. A message published to a stopped topic is
accepted, stored and counted exactly as before \- it is simply held
rather than fanned out, and
.BR euclid-cli-ens-start-topic (1)
hands over everything that was held, oldest first.
.PP
That is the point of stopping a topic rather than unsubscribing from it:
a subscriber being redeployed, or a downstream system taken down for the
evening, is a reason to hold what arrives rather than to lose it. The
publisher does not have to know, and does not have to stop.
.SH WHAT IT DOES NOT DO
It does not touch the subscriptions, which are still there and still
listed by
.BR euclid-cli-ens-list-subscriptions (1).
It does not stop other topics: this is one topic's delivery, not the
module's.
.PP
And it does not suspend retention. A held message expires like any
other, so a topic left stopped for longer than its retention period \-
fourteen days unless it says otherwise, see
.BR euclid-cli-ens-set-topic-retention (1)
\- loses what it was holding, oldest first. Stopping a topic is for
hours and days, not for months.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic " " \fINAME\fR
Topic name. A full ERN also works, and is what reaches another
namespace. Required.
.SH SEEING IT
A stopped topic reports
.I STOPPED
as its status, which
.BR euclid-cli-ens-list-topics (1)
prints for every topic and
.BR euclid-cli-ens-get-topic-metadata (1)
prints alongside
.IR held ,
the number of messages waiting for the topic to be started again.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The topic is stopped; its ERN and status are printed. Stopping one that
is already stopped does nothing and is not an error.
.TP
.B 1
No topic of that name.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
# While the consumer is redeployed
euclid-cli ens stop-topic --topic orders
euclid-cli ens start-topic --topic orders

# What it is holding
euclid-cli ens list-messages --topic orders
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-start-topic (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-set-topic-retention (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-list-subscriptions (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-publish-message (1)
